  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "New Millport earned its name when a post office opened in 1855, adding “New” to avoid confusion with another Millport in Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first sawmill on Little Clearfield Creek, built between 1820 and 1825, still stands as a reminder of the town’s milling roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the Beech Creek Railroad reached New Millport in 1885, the village sprouted general stores, a short‑lived brewery, and small coal pits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "New Millport Methodist Episcopal Church, organized around 1845, and the first schoolhouse, built circa 1842, marked the town’s early commitment to faith and learning.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Little Clearfield Creek, a 14.5‑mile tributary of Clearfield Creek, has long defined New Millport’s landscape and powered its early mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, New Millport remains a quiet, agriculture‑and resource‑oriented community within the DuBois micropolitan area, preserving its rural character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/new_millport_pennsylvania",
